  "design_decision": "Class-weighted model selected over unweighted despite near-identical macro F1 (0.96 both), because it improves recall on minority attack classes (Bots: 0.89->0.95, Web Attacks: 0.93->0.97) at the cost of precision (more false positives on Normal Traffic). This reflects real-world IDS priorities where false negatives (missed attacks) carry substantially higher cost than false positives (extra analyst review), consistent with standard security operations practice.",
  "confusion_note": "Primary confusion for Bots class is bidirectional with Normal Traffic (not with other attack types), consistent with botnet C2 traffic often mimicking low-and-slow benign traffic patterns to evade detection."
